out=['<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>V35 · What the story gives Roshan</title><style>'+css+'</style><header><p>Mermaid Roshan · editorial development review · V35 proposal</p><h1>What does Roshan carry out of the castle?</h1><p class="lead">Fantasy, visual humour and family warmth already give this book value. The next draft can give its heroine a clearer learning journey: notice a need, help gently, accept help, and make room for a friend.</p><p class="notice">Proposal only. The current V34 manuscript, pages and PDFs remain unchanged. One owner question is pending: kindness first, small-step confidence first, or equal weight? The cover candidates below are new review layouts; no whole new narrative scene was drawn.</p><p><a href="../v34_editorial_polish/complete/READ_BOOK.html">Read V34</a> · <a href="story_review.json">Complete proposal and sources</a> · <a href="cover_proposal.json">Cover sources and transforms</a> · <a href="generation_evidence.json">ImageGen prompt and provenance</a></p></header>']
out+=['<section><h2>The stronger emotional arc</h2><p>At first the castle looks like too much. Daddy helps Roshan choose a beginning. She learns that cleaning can make play comfortable and let someone move freely. When play hurts a friend, she notices that friend’s point of view. At the last door, she hears a need instead of treating a dusty stranger as an enemy. This time she asks her friends for help. The final reward is feeling better and being included.</p><p>This is an editorial proposal using the existing scenes. It preserves the finished kindness plot and the rainbow surprise. It does not add a new quest, a failure episode, a new medical diagnosis or a sermon after each room.</p></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>Rear cover: promise the beginning</h2><div class="grid"><figure><h3>A · Recommended: at the threshold</h3><a href="REAR_A.html"><img src="proofs/rear_A.png" alt="Spoiler-free entrance rear-cover draft"></a><p>Roshan and Daddy face the castle together. The blurb asks where to begin. The ending stays inside the book.</p></figure><figure><h3>B · Alternative: the arrival</h3><a href="REAR_B.html"><img src="proofs/rear_B.png" alt="Spoiler-free arrival rear-cover draft"></a><p>More room for the setting and a quiet question. Less character connection than A.</p></figure></div><p class="source">Both use complete existing source scenes. A adds only a tiny source-bound character isolation. These are cover-review candidates, not an updated book export.</p></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>What the existing draft leaves on the table</h2><div class="grid">'+''.join('<article><h3>'+esc(q['issue'])+'</h3><p>'+esc(q['evidence'])+'</p><p>'+esc(q['change'])+'</p></article>' for q in diagnosis)+'</div></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>One story, several kinds of value</h2><table><tr><th>Layer</th><th>What it offers</th><th>How the story carries it</th><th>Restraint</th></tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(q[k])+'</td>' for k in ['layer','aim','vehicle','limit'])+'</tr>' for q in learning)+'</table></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>Concrete wording to discuss</h2><p>These are proposed lines, not proofread final layouts. The other twenty interior pages keep their current captions. Page 20 also proposes replacing the explanatory second bubble with a promise to play gently; that changes prior exact owner wording and remains pending.</p><table><tr><th>Page</th><th>Current</th><th>Proposed</th><th>Purpose / art scope</th></tr>'+''.join('<tr><td>'+str(q['page'])+'</td><td><pre>'+esc(q['before'])+'</pre></td><td><pre>'+esc(q['proposed'])+'</pre></td><td><b>'+esc(q['learning'])+'</b><p>'+esc(q['reason'])+'</p><small>'+esc(q['art_scope'])+'</small></td></tr>' for q in rows)+'</table></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>Learning through a reread</h2><p>A separate grown-up card can offer one optional invitation per reread. The child can point, act, answer briefly or keep enjoying the story. These prompts would live outside the 34 story pages.</p><table><tr><th>Pages</th><th>Invitation</th><th>Everyday connection</th></tr>'+''.join('<tr><td>'+q['pages']+'</td><td>'+esc(q['prompt'])+'</td><td>'+esc(q['transfer'])+'</td></tr>' for q in prompts)+'</table><p>The refrains can support joining in now and familiarity later. They should not be presented as a phonics programme or proof that Roshan is decoding unfamiliar words.</p></section>']
out+=['<section><h2>What the guidance supports</h2>'+''.join('<article><h3><a href="'+q['url']+'">'+esc(q['title'])+'</a></h3><p>'+esc(q['supported'])+'</p><p class="source">Our proposed application: '+esc(q['application'])+'</p></article><br>' for q in sources)+'<p>These sources inform the editorial design. A finished book still needs real read-aloud observation and owner/child acceptance; the review does not establish professional SLP approval.</p><h2>Decision before rewriting</h2><p>The recommended emphasis is kindness through attentive action, with the small-jobs refrain as a tool for acting on that kindness. The pending owner response will determine how much the opening and closing lean into confidence versus perspective-taking.</p></section>']
write(V/'STORY_REVIEW.html',''.join(out))
